/-!
# Exact stored endpoints for the actual radius-two head

The 65-by-65 signed head table has denominator `2^44`: 64 physical
coordinates followed by the scalar pole. It is the retained head used by
`RadiusTwoPaidObservedGridReturn`, with physical shift `-1/2` and the
unshifted scalar corner `1/2`. The pinned endpoint JSON SHA-256 is
`de9920657b407c08fde02320f919198c18fe277d0e5c02cb731a77b5ad0bf5fd`.
Biased 64-bit words encode signed endpoint numerators only. The separate
core compares the actual stored scalar observations by exact integer
endpoint formulas; bounded groups check all literal table entries.
No raw reconstruction product, remote enclosure, high floor, paid sign,
cofinal theorem, RH or GRH is supplied by these head data. Independent
analytical review and novelty assessment remain pending. Formal evidence
is source-bound and recorded separately by Noe.
-/
